  "description": "Starting from the building's IFC model, IfcOpenShell extracts the geometry, spaces and construction build-ups; a zone take-off turns those into an EnergyPlus whole-building model for design-grade energy and comfort, plus a parallel Modelica RC reduced-order model that is fast enough to run in the loop. Both are calibrated against a few weeks of BMS and sub-metering data with a Bayesian step, so the twin tracks the building as operated rather than as drawn.\n\nThe calibrated twin drives a model-predictive controller that proposes HVAC set-points from forecast weather and occupancy, and raises an alert when measured behaviour drifts from prediction. Everything lands in a historian for continuous re-calibration. Budget roughly EUR 40-90k for a single mid-size building (IFC clean-up, calibration campaign, BMS integration); expect 10-16 weeks to a live twin giving read-only control advice, longer for closed-loop write-back.\n\nIllustrative output — a saved generation shown for display only, not a delivered project.",
